"},{"date":"2026-10-22","committee":"Council","time":"5.00 pm","status":"New; Special","webcast":false,"url":"https://moderngov.fareham.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-10-22","committee":"Council","time":"6.00 pm","status":"New; Moved from 15 October 2026","webcast":false,"url":"https://moderngov.fareham.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-10-26","committee":"Overview and Scrutiny Board","time":"6.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://moderngov.fareham.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-11-02","committee":"Executive","time":"5.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://moderngov.fareham.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-11-23","committee":"Audit and Governance Committee","time":"6.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://moderngov.fareham.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-12-03","committee":"PfSH Overview and Scrutiny Committee (Dates Only)","time":"10.30 am","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://moderngov.fareham.gov.uk"}],"recent":[{"date":"2026-07-31","committee":"Executive Portfolio for Leisure and Community","time":"10.00 am","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://moderngov.fareham.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-02","committee":"Overview and Scrutiny Board","time":"6.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://moderngov.fareham.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-07","committee":"Executive","time":"5.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://moderngov.fareham.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-08","committee":"Audit and Governance Committee","time":"6.00 pm","status":"New; Moved from 8 June 2026","webcast":false,"url":"https://moderngov.fareham.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-16","committee":"PfSH Overview and Scrutiny Committee (Dates Only)","time":"10.30 am","status":"Cancelled","webcast":false,"url":"https://moderngov.fareham.gov.uk"}]},"news":[],"news_drafts":[{"headline":"Awaab's Law (effective October 2025) introduced statutory repair timescales for social housing; council recruited new Property Inspector role.","lead":"New regulatory duties create operational costs and compliance risk; failure to meet statutory timescales could trigger enforcement action and damage the council's credibility as a housing provider.","iso":"2026-07-27","paper_title":"Appendix D - Draft Annual Governance Statement","paper_url":"https://fareham.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s49851/49851.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true},{"headline":"Medium-term funding gaps in 2027/28 and 2028/29 will require drawing down Council reserves to address shortfalls.","lead":"Planned reserve drawdown indicates liquidity constraint and reduces financial flexibility to respond to emergencies, service pressures, or unexpected costs.","iso":"2026-07-27","paper_title":"Appendix D - Draft Annual Governance Statement","paper_url":"https://fareham.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s49851/49851.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true},{"headline":"Four additional control area weaknesses identified requiring enhancement including purchasing card authorisation","lead":"Multiple identified control deficiencies across different functions indicate broader governance maturity issues affecting financial stewardship and compliance.","iso":"2026-07-27","paper_title":"Chief Internal Auditors Annual Opinion 2025-26","paper_url":"https://fareham.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s49818/49818.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true}],"findings":[{"iso":"2026-07-27","committee":"Audit and Governance Committee","paper_title":"Appendix D - Draft Annual Governance Statement","paper_url":"https://fareham.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s49851/49851.pdf","headline":"Awaab's Law (effective October 2025) introduced statutory repair timescales for social housing; council recruited new Property Inspector role.","detail":"Awaab's Law came into effect in October 2025 and introduced statutory timescales for social housing repairs, particularly for damp and mould, with requirements for tenant communication throughout repair stages. Fareham responded by recruiting a new Property Inspector to review housing stock and ensure timely resolution of damp and mould issues.","category":"governance","matters":"New regulatory duties create operational costs and compliance risk; failure to meet statutory timescales could trigger enforcement action and damage the council's credibility as a housing provider.","figures":"One new Property Inspector position created; statute effective October 2025","quote":"A new Property Inspector has been recruited, and they will have responsibility for accurately reviewing the Council's Housing stock and documenting cases of damp and mould to ensure they are resolved in a timely manner.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-07-27","committee":"Audit and Governance Committee","paper_title":"Appendix D - Draft Annual Governance Statement","paper_url":"https://fareham.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s49851/49851.pdf","headline":"Medium-term funding gaps in 2027/28 and 2028/29 will require drawing down Council reserves to address shortfalls.","detail":"The Medium Term Financial Strategy for 2025-2030 predicts funding gaps in both 2027/28 and 2028/29, with government funding expected to help balance the budget only by 2029/30. The council will need to use reserves to support the Local Government Reorganisation programme through April 2028, and further projects are anticipated to require additional reserve depletion to address shortfalls in the next two years.","category":"reserves","matters":"Planned reserve drawdown indicates liquidity constraint and reduces financial flexibility to respond to emergencies, service pressures, or unexpected costs.","figures":"Funding gaps in 2027/28 and 2028/29; reserves required through April 2028 for LGR; \u00a3271,000 savings in 2025/26 from Opportunities Plan","quote":"Going forward, there will be a requirement to use Council reserves to support the LGR programme through to April 2028. The current Opportunities Plan will still need to be used to address the shortfall in the next two financial years.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-07-27","committee":"Audit and Governance Committee","paper_title":"Chief Internal Auditors Annual Opinion 2025-26","paper_url":"https://fareham.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s49818/49818.pdf","headline":"Four additional control area weaknesses identified requiring enhancement including purchasing card authorisation","detail":"The audit opinion identifies specific governance gaps requiring remediation: vehicle record maintenance in Streetscene, controls over repair invoice verification, purchasing card authorisation processes, and VAT treatment consistency. These gaps span procurement, asset management and financial processes.","category":"governance","matters":"Multiple identified control deficiencies across different functions indicate broader governance maturity issues affecting financial stewardship and compliance.","figures":"4 priority areas identified","quote":"Additional areas noted this year where further action will enhance the adequacy and effectiveness of governance, risk management and control include: a. Maintenance of records relating to vehicles within the Streetscene Directorate b. Controls and processes for the calculation and verification of repairs invoices c. The authorisation process for purchasing cards d. Greater clarity and consistency on the treatment of VAT","material":true},{"iso":"2026-07-27","committee":"Audit and Governance Committee","paper_title":"Chief Internal Auditors Annual Opinion 2025-26","paper_url":"https://fareham.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s49818/49818.pdf","headline":"Audit recommendation implementation rate fell to 56% from 74%, with 35% still in progress","detail":"Of 108 essential or important recommendations reviewed, only 56% have been implemented or closed, with 35% in progress. This is a material decline from 2024/25 when 74% were implemented. The council has introduced action-by dates for new recommendations in attempt to improve completion rates.","category":"audit","matters":"Low recommendation implementation rates extend exposure to identified control weaknesses. Declining performance suggests services are slower to remediate issues and weaker accountability for control improvement.","figures":"56% implemented vs 74% prior year; 35% in progress; 108 recommendations reviewed","quote":"Of the 108 recommendations reviewed 56% of recommendations followed up were signed off by the audit team and a further 35% were being progressed. This represents a drop in performance from the previous year.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-07-27","committee":"Audit and Governance Committee","paper_title":"Chief Internal Auditors Annual Opinion 2025-26","paper_url":"https://fareham.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s49818/49818.pdf","headline":"Payroll system error caused \u00a32,117 overpayment to elected members that only audit detected","detail":"The system applied both a Councillor Allowance and Employee Allowance simultaneously to three elected members in August 2025, resulting in a \u00a32,117 overpayment. The error was only identified through audit testing, suggesting insufficient reconciliation controls in payroll.","category":"overspend","matters":"Payroll overpayments represent direct cash loss and indicate control gaps in routine financial systems. That audit was needed to identify the error suggests weak preventive controls.","figures":"\u00a32,117 overpayment in single pay run","quote":"The Payroll, Pensions and Employee Expenses audit noted 1 error. This related to the overpayment to three elected members in the August 2025 pay run as the system had applied both a Councillor and Employee Allowance in error. The total value of the overpayment was \u00a32,117.","material":false}],"editorial":null,"freshness":{"last_paper_iso":"2026-07-27"},"name":"Fareham","findings_total":41,"news_drafts_total":3}}